<%#
  What a dashboard section says before the buyer has done the thing. Always
  carries the link that fills it — an empty section that only says "nothing here"
  leaves the buyer to go and find the shop themselves.

  Given the same card as the filled state, because this is not an error: every
  sign-in lands on this page, so for a new account this IS the dashboard, and a
  bare grey sentence read as a page that had failed to load. The CTA is a real
  pill at py-4 rather than the 19px inline link it used to be — this page's
  reader is meant to hit it one-handed, in the dark.

  locals: body, label, href, icon
%>
<div class="mb-11 flex flex-col items-start gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-border-strong bg-surface px-5.5 py-6">
  <span class="text-t3 leading-none" aria-hidden="true"><%= icon %></span>

  <p class="text-t5 text-tan m-0"><%= body %></p>

  <%= render Buttons::Component.new(
    text: label,
    href: href,
    pill: true,
    variant: :secondary,
    classes: "hover:cursor-pointer text-t6! font-bold! py-4 px-6"
  ) %>
</div>
